hooks/diff.ts is adapted from Replay Theater, a mod in claude-code-playground:

  Replay Theater, Copyright 2026 Anthropic PBC. Apache License 2.0.
  https://github.com/anthropics/claude-code-playground

The line diff (an LCS table with a fallback for long inputs) and the context
trimming come from it. filetrail types them for TypeScript, makes the context
width a parameter and adds a cap on the lines kept.

hooks/row.tsx follows the approach of claude-code-filetree's hooks/rows.tsx:
tree rows drawn by a surface module (a Client) in plain Text, so their colours
paint on the desktop, with the press taken from onPointer and sent to the hooks
module by post. filetrail draws one Client per row and keeps its own row model.
The shimmer's band and palettes, and the git verbs and tones of the git bar
(hooks/git-actions.ts), follow the same mod.

  claude-code-filetree, Copyright (c) 2026 Kurt Buhler. MIT License.
  https://github.com/data-goblin/claude-code-filetree

The rest of filetrail is written from scratch. Its file tree was also inspired
by the feature set of claude-code-filetree.

